# ── Docker build context ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sent to the daemon before the build starts, so anything listed here is neither
# uploaded nor able to bust a layer cache. Keeping it small matters more than it
# looks: the build context for this monorepo is every workspace, including
# `node_modules` (hundreds of megabytes from Expo/React Native) and `.git`.

# Installed inside the image from the lockfile. Copying a host `node_modules` in
# would import the host's platform binaries — the classic "works on my machine,
# `Error: invalid ELF header` in CI" failure.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output, rebuilt in the image.
**/dist
.turbo
**/.expo
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios

# Secrets. `apps/api/.env` holds real credentials and must never enter an image
# layer — layers are pushed to a registry and readable by anyone who can pull it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# VCS and editor state.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Local cache/log noise.
*.log
.DS_Store
